**2. Create `.claude/hooks/format-bash-writes.sh`** (make it executable with `chmod +x`):

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

cd "$(jq -r '.cwd' <<<"$(cat)")"

# Files git considers modified or new. Filter to ones that exist (deletions drop out).
{ git diff --name-only HEAD; git ls-files --others --exclude-standard; } \
  | sort -u \
  | while IFS= read -r f; do [ -f "$f" ] && printf '%s\n' "$f"; done \
